{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal setup combining RNA (scvi_n200) and image (ViT-L) data with transformer aggregation and concat fusion, building on a strong RNA-only baseline (0.653 accuracy). Validation accuracy improved to 0.7207 and F1 to 0.6815, suggesting multimodal fusion may enhance performance. Uncertainty remains about the relative contribution of image modality versus other factors like fusion strategy or encoder interactions, as no direct comparisons to alternative modalities or fusion methods were conducted."
}

